(densified copy of a lathe record array, for the level-crossing scans only)
()
(lathe_level_pass and lathe_level_next_start decide where a roughing pass stops)
(by walking the record array and reading ONLY each record's endpoint - fields)
(+0 and +1. An arc record therefore reaches them as the straight chord joining)
(its two endpoints, and the offset-crossing test runs against that chord. For a)
(convex arc the chord lies inside the material, so the level crosses it later)
(than it crosses the real radius and the pass keeps cutting past the profile:)
(the error is the arc's sagitta, R*[1 - COS[sweep/2]], minus the roughing)
(allowance, so it stays hidden on small radii and gouges once the radius grows.)
()
(This sub rewrites every arc as short straight sub-records whose endpoints lie)
(ON the true arc, subdivided until the residual sagitta is below max_sag. The)
(scans then stop at the radius itself, with a bounded and knowable error, and)
(their own logic - segment offsetting, corner connectors, the multi-crossing)
(walk - is left completely untouched.)
()
(Only the scans use this copy. The contour passes keep reading the original)
(array, so lathe_poly_pass/trace_lathe still emit true G2/G3 arcs and the)
(dynamic cutter compensation they depend on is unaffected.)
o<poly_mesh_lathe> sub
(CALL src[1] dst[2] max_sag[3])

	#<src>     = #1
	#<dst>     = #2
	#<max_sag> = #3

	#[#<dst>] = 0
	#<rec_n>  = #[#<src>]

	(first record is the profile start point - no segment leads into it)
	#<sp> = [#<src> + 1]
	o<add_mill_data> CALL [#<dst>] [#[#<sp>]] [#[#<sp> + 1]] [#[#<sp> + 2]] [#[#<sp> + 3]] [#[#<sp> + 4]] [#[#<sp> + 5]] [#[#<sp> + 6]] [#[#<sp> + 7]]

	#<pz> = #[#<sp>]
	#<pr> = #[#<sp> + 1]
	#<rp> = [#<src> + 9]
	#<i>  = 1

	o<mesh_00> while [#<i> LT #<rec_n>]
		#<i>   = [#<i> + 1]
		#<cz>  = #[#<rp>]
		#<cr>  = #[#<rp> + 1]
		#<dir> = #[#<rp> + 2]
		#<ccz> = #[#<rp> + 3]
		#<ccr> = #[#<rp> + 4]

		(arc records carry the G-code word itself in dir: 2 = G2, 3 = G3.)
		(anything else - rapid or straight - is copied through unchanged)
		#<is_arc> = 0
		o<arc_chk> if [[#<dir> EQ 2] OR [#<dir> EQ 3]]
			#<rad> = SQRT[[#<pz> - #<ccz>] * [#<pz> - #<ccz>] + [#<pr> - #<ccr>] * [#<pr> - #<ccr>]]
			o<rad_ok> if [[#<rad> GT #<max_sag>] AND [#<rad> GT 0.0001]]
				#<is_arc> = 1
			o<rad_ok> endif
		o<arc_chk> endif

		o<seg> if [#<is_arc> EQ 0]
			o<add_mill_data> CALL [#<dst>] [#<cz>] [#<cr>] [#<dir>] [#<ccz>] [#<ccr>] [#[#<rp> + 5]] [#[#<rp> + 6]] [#[#<rp> + 7]]
		o<seg> else
			(angles of the two endpoints about the centre, in the [Z, radius])
			(plane. dir 3 - G3 - sweeps toward increasing angle here, dir 2 the)
			(other way; verified against the canon rotation flag of a real arc)
			#<a1> = ATAN[#<pr> - #<ccr>]/[#<pz> - #<ccz>]
			#<a2> = ATAN[#<cr> - #<ccr>]/[#<cz> - #<ccz>]
			o<sw_dir> if [#<dir> EQ 3]
				o<sw_up> while [#<a2> LE #<a1>]
					#<a2> = [#<a2> + 360]
				o<sw_up> endwhile
			o<sw_dir> else
				o<sw_dn> while [#<a2> GE #<a1>]
					#<a2> = [#<a2> - 360]
				o<sw_dn> endwhile
			o<sw_dir> endif
			#<sweep> = [#<a2> - #<a1>]

			(step angle that keeps each sub-chord's own sagitta under max_sag:)
			(sag = rad * [1 - COS[step/2]]  ->  step = 2 * ACOS[1 - sag/rad])
			#<step> = [2 * ACOS[1 - [#<max_sag> / #<rad>]]]
			o<step_ok> if [#<step> LT 0.05]
				#<step> = 0.05
			o<step_ok> endif
			#<steps> = FUP[ABS[#<sweep>] / #<step>]
			o<steps_ok> if [#<steps> LT 1]
				#<steps> = 1
			o<steps_ok> endif
			(hard cap per arc. The mesh array is laid out past the reversed)
			(one and the polyline's own item records live from 4982 down, so)
			(an arc-heavy profile subdividing without limit could eventually)
			(run into them. 64 sub-records holds a full semicircle to well)
			(under 0.01 mm; beyond that the residual grows but stays far)
			(below the chord error this whole sub exists to remove)
			o<steps_cap> if [#<steps> GT 64]
				#<steps> = 64
			o<steps_cap> endif

			#<k> = 1
			o<mesh_arc> while [#<k> LT #<steps>]
				#<ang> = [#<a1> + #<sweep> * #<k> / #<steps>]
				o<add_mill_data> CALL [#<dst>] [[#<ccz> + #<rad> * COS[#<ang>]]] [[#<ccr> + #<rad> * SIN[#<ang>]]] [1] [0] [0] [0] [0] [0]
				#<k> = [#<k> + 1]
			o<mesh_arc> endwhile

			(land the last sub-record on the record's own endpoint exactly,)
			(so the mesh cannot drift away from the profile it came from)
			o<add_mill_data> CALL [#<dst>] [#<cz>] [#<cr>] [1] [0] [0] [0] [0] [0]
		o<seg> endif

		#<pz> = #<cz>
		#<pr> = #<cr>
		#<rp> = [#<rp> + 8]
	o<mesh_00> endwhile

o<poly_mesh_lathe> endsub
